1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,020
Good morning. Stretton Festival box office. How can I help you?

2
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:10,433
Oh, hello. My family and I are on holiday in the area,

3
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:14,110
and we've seen some posters about the festival this week.

4
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:17,290
Could you tell me about some of the events, please?

5
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:18,210
Of course.

6
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:23,810
First of all, are there still tickets available for the jazz band on Saturday?

7
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:30,410
There are, but only 15 pounds. The 12-pound seats have all been sold.

8
00:00:30,410 --> 00:00:34,380
OK. And the venue is the school, isn't it?

9
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,100
Yes, that's right, the secondary school.

10
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:41,020
Make sure you don't go to the primary school by mistake!

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,960
And there's an additional performer

12
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:48,780
who isn't mentioned on the posters -Carolyn Hart is going to play with the band.

13
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,000
Oh, I think I've heard her on the radio

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,170
Doesn't she play the oboe, or flute or something?

15
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:57,604
Yes, the flute. She usually plays with symphony orchestras,

16
00:00:57,604 --> 00:01:01,800
and apparently this is her first time with a jazz band.

17
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,990
Well, I'd certainly like to hear her.

18
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:08,107
Then the next thing I want to ask about is the duck races -

19
00:01:08,107 --> 00:01:11,590
I saw a poster beside a river. What are they, exactly?

20
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:18,470
Well, you buy a yellow plastic duck - or as many as you like - they're a pound each.

21
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:21,180
And you write your name on each one.

22
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:26,180
There'll be several races, depending on the number of ducks taking part.

23
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:32,520
And John Stevens, a champion swimmer who lives locally, is going to start the races.

24
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:37,320
All the ducks will be launched into the river at the back of the cinema,

25
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:42,120
then they'll float along the river for 500 metres, as far as the railway bridge.

26
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,000
And are there any prizes?

27
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:53,350
Yes, the first duck in each race to arrive at the finishing line wins its owner free tickets for the concert on the last night of the festival.

28
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:57,990
You said you can buy a duck? I'm sure my children will both want one.

29
00:01:57,990 --> 00:02:00,610
They're on sale at a stall in the market.

30
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:04,770
You can't miss it - it's got an enormous sign showing a couple of ducks.

31
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:09,860
OK. I'll go there this afternoon. I remember walking past there yesterday.

32
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:13,800
Now could you tell me something about the flower show, please?

33
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:20,200
Well, admission is free, and the show is being held in Bythwaite Hall.

34
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:22,140
Sorry, how do you spell that?

35
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:30,370
B-Y-T-H-W-A-I-T-E. Bythwaite.

36
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:35,110
Is it easy to find? I'm not very familiar with the town yet.

37
00:02:35,110 --> 00:02:39,890
Oh, you won't have any problem. It's right in the centre of Stretton.

38
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:44,450
It's the only old building in the town, so it's easy to recognise.

39
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:47,520
I know it. I presume it's open all day.

40
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:52,380
Yes, but if you'd like to see the prizes being awarded for the best flowers

41
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,930
you'll need to there at 5 o'clock.

42
00:02:54,930 --> 00:03:00,030
The prizes are being given by a famous actor Kevin Shapless.

43
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:04,030
He lives nearby and gets involved in a lot of community events.

44
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:07,840
Gosh, I've seen him on TV. I'll definitely go to the prize-giving.

45
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,770
Right.

46
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:13,257
I've seen a list of plays that are being performed this week,

47
00:03:13,257 --> 00:03:18,400
and I'd like to know which are suitable for my children

48
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:21,110
and which ones my husband and I might go to.

49
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:22,570
How old are your children?

50
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:26,510
Five and seven. What about 'The Mystery of Muldoon'?

51
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:28,860
That's aimed at five to ten-year-olds.

52
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:32,950
So if I take my children, I can expect them to enjoy it more than I do?

53
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:37,304
I think so. If you'd like something for yourself and your husband,

54
00:03:37,304 --> 00:03:42,746
and leave your children with a babysitter, you might like to see 'Fire and Flood' -

55
00:03:42,746 --> 00:03:47,100
it's about events that really happened in Stretton two hundred years ago,

56
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:49,640
and children might find it rather frightening.

57
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:54,910
Oh, thanks for the warning. And finally, what about 'Silly Sailor'?

58
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:57,844
That's a comedy, and it's for young and old.

59
00:03:57,844 --> 00:04:03,060
In fact, it won an award in the Stretton Drama Festival a couple of months ago.

60
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:06,560
OK. Well, goodbye, and thanks for all the information

61
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:08,560
I'm looking forward to the festival!

62
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,810
Goodbye.
